we've finally decided to discard, and it pains me to see it not end up
in the hands of someone interested in such machines as opposed to a
Colorado landfill.  This machine performed historic firsts in data
processing of coherent laser radar data that we collected back in ~
1988-1990 roughly.  I can find out more about it soon for those
interested.  It was very high end at the time for our specific needs,
so I suspect it's pretty loaded up with good stuff.  Probably a pile of
manuals in the storage locker, too.  My office manager said we might
even crate it up (with one of the jillions of crates we have that we
ALSO need to discard from the relevant storage locker...), so an
across-country enterprise here might not be completely out of the
question.  Anyhow, I thought I'd start here and see if there was any
interest.  By all means let anyone else you might know, know about it,
too.  I sure don't want to see it end up in an artificial reef
someplace, you know?  Thanks.

