Have you considered white box alpha's? If you're looking for a hobbyist
system, where support is not an issue, then white box alpha's may be
more attractive. These systems were meant to run only Windows, and
Windows NT only at that. These systems are dumped at fairly low prices,
sometimes they're available for free.
The Digital Server models 3000, 5305 and 7305 are similar to the Alpha
Server 800, 1200 and 4100.
Two things worth considering:
1) A small software modification is required, easily found on the web
2) the 5305 and 7305 come with (pci) SCSI controllers that are not
supported by VMS,  the embedded SCSI-2 controller is supported by VMS
so the CDROM and and hard disk will work. The 3000 has an on board
UW-SCSI controler that is supported by VMS.



