I'm running VMS on a 500au with an Elsa Gloria Synergy card.  The VMS
drivers do not support video capture on that card even though there's
hardware for it, but it works fine for output (although I never tested the
S-video out, only the VGA).  Despite the "wasted" capture capability, that
card is actually the cheapest (based on my own search) for doing hi-res
graphics on VMS.

Other cards I have seen in Alphastations include video cards with a 1/8"
output for 3-D glasses and audio cards with RCA jacks.

