Since I started this I will put in my 2 cents.
As I understand it HP has stated that a hobbyiest may obtain the
software by any means possible,  buying it, borrowing it or have a
total stranger make copies with no control or questions. The way I see
it those words obtain the software opens a ftp site. No where in the
by-laws does it state that one must obtain the software from a
authorize site or person. I offered the software only and I hope that
most of the hundred or so people where hobbyiest. I didnot make a penny
off the service, nor did I ask for any money. If HP was so concern
about losing money then they need to clarify or put in laws just where
can a hobbyiest obtain the software. At no time did I offer anyway for
a person to run the software (ie the PAKS). I am not a lawyer,  but the
way I see it someone would be hard-press to say I am doing something
illegal when I can give copies away with no control. No where does it
state that the copies cannot be electronic in nature for the hobbyiest.
Since there is no way to check to make sure the person is a hobbyiest
then the site must be open. I know I did not make it clear that the
software was for non-commerical use only.   I will say this that sooner
or later somebody else is going to offer the software via ftp so maybe
HP needs to step in and clear this up. 
just my 2cents



