Following up my own post here, just in case someone in the future does 
some research into the same question.  I'll post more when I know more.

Apparently the VAXstation 4000 60, 90 and 90A all use the same type of
memory, either 4 MB (54-19145-AU or 54-19103-AA) or 16 MB (54-19103-CA); 
the 60 has 3 pairs of banks and the 90 and 90A have 2 groups of 4 banks.

I'll investigate the VAX 4000 and VAXstation 3100 models next.  :-)

While researching this (newsgroup archives, used-equipment dealers and
my own experiments), I was reminded that VAX memory used to cost about
$100 per MB.  :-) 



