VAXstation 3100/30, /38, /40, /48 use the same memory cards, as do the 
MicroVAX 3100-10, 10e, 20, and 20e.  There used to be 4, 8, 12, and 16MB 
cards from DEC (perhaps other sizes from other vendors); the 8 and 16MB 
cards had dual connectors that allowed a second single port (4, 12MB) 
card to be installed, or a single port card could be installed directly 
to the main logic board.  32MB maximum with 4MB embedded, 16MB dual 
port, and 12MB single port installed.

My 3100-30 at work has a 16 and a 12 for 32MB maximum memory.

Rich


