"Phillip Helbig---remove CLOTHES to reply" <helbig@astro.multiCLOTHESvax.de> wrote in message
news:das71l$ut2$1@online.de...

> Of course, when actually using the system, rather than just testing, I
> would do an AUTOGEN regularly anyway, especially after changing the
> memory configuration, whether it is "needed" or not.  However, out of
> curiosity, does VMS automatically detect decreased memory but not
> increased memory?

Generally AUTOGEN sets PHYSICALPAGES to the amount of memory
in the system, so yes. There were some pathological cases where you could
make a system so badly out of tune, by throwing huge quantities of memory
at it, that it would not boot. This behaviour was added to AUTOGEN
late in the VAX era when you could buy memory in big chunks.
None of the above applies to Alpha.




