the larger sizes during the 60s-70s, so many publishers almost
abolished UC usage on the book cover. Eg DEC, one of the larger tech
publishers.   Alternatively, noting that the largest lettering was
"FORTRAN" and "pdp", respectively, both in a "hollow" outline font,
perhaps some need to economise on printer's ink.   

