Jeremy Begg wrote:
> Hi,
>
> I have recently acquired an AlphaServer 800 with 1GB RAM and four 9GB
> drives.  I'd like to get the maximum possible performance out of the
> internal drives but I notice that the internal CD-ROM drive is also on this
> bus and therefore won't all I/O be done using "narrow" SCSI?
>
> I found the internal hard disk cage and CD-ROM drives have separate SCSI
> cables to the motherboard.  Is it possible that the on-board SCSI controller
> is capable of driving the hard drives using wide SCSI and the CD-ROM with
> narrow SCSI, at the same time?
>
> Thanks,
>
> 	Jeremy Begg
> 	jeremy-at-vsm-dot-com-au
>

Jeremy,

  According to the Alphaserver 800 User's Guide (page 9-1):

 "The SCSI bus can be configured with any mix of wide, narrow, fast, or
ULTRA devices.  In a mixed configuration, wide devices run in wide mode
and narrow devices run in narrow mode."

Old user and technical manuals in PDF form and other information is
available on the HP web site at
http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/archive/  Just pick the model you
have from the selector list.



